(II)--a son of उशिज; cursed even in the womb to lose consciousness by बृहस्पति; learnt his धर्म from Saurabheya वृषभ; it was गोधर्म to do as they pleased; once embraced in sexual love his brother's wife; for this he was floated down the Ganges;
1: M. ४८. ४१-57; वा. ९९. ३४-76.
met Vairocana Bali who engaged him for क्षेत्रज sons, five through Bali's queen and one through her servant-maid. This was काक्षीवत्.
2: भा. IX. २३. 5; M. ४८. ५८-78; वा. ९९. ९२.
Surabhi warded him from the darkness clouding him; got the title Gotama;
3: M. ४८. ७९-84.
with काक्षीवत् he went to Girivraja and after penance reached heaven;
4: Ib. ४८. ८५-86.
a ऋषिक and a मन्त्रकृट्.
5: Br. II. ३२. १०१, १११; M. १४५. ९५ and १०५.
